[assigning additional intrinsics to improve other DSM]

On 2003-11-24, Rast <rast2@hotmail.com> wrote:
>
> I like this.  It would be nice if non-silver, non-grey DSM was worth 
> something more than 9 points of AC.  Of course the dragons should get the 
> benefit of the intrinsics as well, so I tried to choose ones that are 
> helpful to monsters.  However, you would not be able to gain these 
> intrinsics by eating dragon meat.
>
> Red dragon scales: Protection and increase damage, +2 in each.  Actual red 
> dragons should get +4 in each -- they are well known for being the most 
> fearsome dragons in combat.

By protection, do you mean it gives additional AC?  Someone suggested
"beige dragons" a long while back which give extra 4 AC, but the
conclusion was that people would still choose GDSM/SDSM, even as an
early wish.  Increase damage is interesting though.

> White dragon scales: Amphibiousness.
>
> Orange dragon scales: Free action.

Orange dragons can be made to breathe paralysis rays for evilness.
Free action will nullify it, and maybe reflection.

> Black dragon scales: Level-drain resistance and hallucination resistance. 

Perhaps give black dragons a drain level bite attack.  Why
hallucination resistance?

> Blue dragon scales: "Very fast" speed.  (If this turns out to be too strong 
> an early wish, make it only "fast" speed.)  Boost the speed rating of blue 
> dragons to 15, from the current 9.

Intrinsic speed is easily obtained by wand or Quantum Mechanic, so
just giving it "fast" will not do much.  "Very fast" will make it VERY
powerful for early wishes though.  How about boosting speed from
normal to fast and fast to very fast?

> Green dragon scales: Hungerless regeneration.  (Can monsters currently get 
> regeneration?) 

Some monsters (trolls) have intrinsic regeneration, and Cyclops may
gain regeneration from wielding the Staff (don't quote me).  I'm not
sure how good regeneration is late game, but would certainly be a
contender for early wishes.

> Yellow dragon scales: Stoning resistance, just like yellow dragons already 
> have.

As before, IMHO, stoning resistance is too powerful.  Stoning is one
of the few ways to kill end-game characters, so I'd keep that.  I
think the problem lies in acidic monsters; that they're rare and the
attacks are mostly passive make them not much of a threat.  Add more
mean acid attacks and it'll be used more.  Maybe an acidic bite...

> Let's also reduce the AC bonus of all DSM to 8, rather than 9.  That's still 
> one more than plate mail/crystal plate mail, which weigh ten times as much.  
> To partially compensate, change the AC of unenchanted scales from 3 to 4.

I'd say reducing DSM's base AC to 8 won't do much.  A typical end game
character has AC between -30 and -40.  IME, values below -30 are
pretty much meaningless.  To make a difference, we'd need to start
chipping away at all the numbers, such as intrinsic protection.  Too
much work, although it may make shields more attractive.

